1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:36,411
<i>You said it yourself,</i>

2
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:40,999
He can adapt to any situation.

3
00:00:41,082 --> 00:00:43,001
<i>And after everything he's been through,</i>

4
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:46,880
<i>he's trained well enough</i>
<i>to excel in combat.</i>

5
00:00:46,963 --> 00:00:49,966
And if you pair him with Chiara,

6
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:52,802
you'll have an incredibly powerful duo.

7
00:00:56,931 --> 00:01:01,186
I just don't want the day to come
when you regret your choice.

8
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:04,105
Because you never told anyone
how you truly felt.

9
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:05,607
I don't mean to interfere,

10
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:06,524
but look at me.

11
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:09,235
After everything I've been through,

12
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,494
You can handle whatever
fate throws your way.

13
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:18,912
But actually, Dad…

14
00:01:18,995 --> 00:01:22,123
<i>I learned something</i>
<i>from everything I've been through.</i>

15
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:23,291
What's that?

16
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:26,002
That my dad is the coolest

17
00:01:26,085 --> 00:01:29,339
and the greatest dad
in the whole wide world!

18
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:32,467
Love you too, son.

19
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:36,888
I like you.

20
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:40,350
I think I've fallen in love with you.

21
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:41,392
Alex?

22
00:01:53,446 --> 00:01:57,117
Let's say it together,
in one, two, three…

23
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,494
We're getting married!

24
00:01:59,577 --> 00:02:00,787
See? I told you!

25
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:03,915
<i>Yes! I'm going to be Mrs. Pinagpala.</i>

26
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:06,000
Oh my gosh, can you believe it?

27
00:02:06,084 --> 00:02:08,878
Honestly, I still can't believe it myself.

28
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:11,548
<i>There's something I want to ask you.</i>

29
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:13,091
Sweetheart, are you okay?

30
00:02:13,174 --> 00:02:14,592
- Can it wait until tomorrow?
- Um, maybe…

31
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:31,276
What?

32
00:02:31,359 --> 00:02:33,069
Me? Your maid of honor?

33
00:02:38,575 --> 00:02:40,743
Chiara, let's talk to Alex tomorrow.

34
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:42,036
No, no, no. Right now.

35
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:46,291
I'm so sorry. I've had a few drinks.

36
00:02:46,374 --> 00:02:47,667
But…

37
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:49,669
Don't worry. Even though I'm tipsy,

38
00:02:49,752 --> 00:02:52,964
<i>my faculties are still intact.</i>

39
00:02:53,047 --> 00:02:56,384
And Alex,
you're the only one who can do it.

40
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:58,511
Only you.

41
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:00,763
I don't really know anyone else here.

42
00:03:01,389 --> 00:03:03,600
And it can't be Carlota.

43
00:03:03,683 --> 00:03:06,144
She's my dad's Chihuahua.

44
00:03:10,982 --> 00:03:13,026
Please, it has to be you.

45
00:03:20,366 --> 00:03:21,743
Let me know, okay?

46
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:27,540
He gave this to me.

47
00:03:30,793 --> 00:03:32,629
<i>It's so light.</i>

48
00:03:32,712 --> 00:03:33,838
It's adorable.

49
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:38,051
That's okay because I'm
so deeply in love with you.

50
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:40,803
<i>Chiara, come back here!</i>

51
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:42,430
- <i>We still have to vlog.</i>
- <i>Okay.</i>

52
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:43,932
Hey, come dance with us.

53
00:03:44,015 --> 00:03:45,934
- Why don't you join our vlog, Alex?
- Come on!

54
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:46,893
Come on!

55
00:03:46,976 --> 00:03:48,519
Let's dance! Come on!

56
00:03:49,062 --> 00:03:51,981
Hey!

57
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,531
All right, bye.

58
00:05:03,052 --> 00:05:04,512
My head hurts.

59
00:05:07,181 --> 00:05:08,641
I have a headache.

60
00:05:08,725 --> 00:05:10,768
Oh no. Are you okay? What happened?

61
00:05:12,895 --> 00:05:14,314
I feel dizzy.

62
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:17,025
Come here. Easy now.

63
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:22,447
- Can I have--
- Mikoy and Chiara are getting married?

64
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,365
You're going to give me a heart attack!

65
00:05:24,449 --> 00:05:25,658
Where did you come from?

66
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:29,120
And… How did you find out?

67
00:05:30,204 --> 00:05:33,207
Well, I'm friends with Captain Pepe,

68
00:05:33,291 --> 00:05:35,209
Dekyo, and Janjan on Fishbook.

69
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:36,836
I saw their posts.

70
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:38,755
Right after your brother proposed.

71
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:41,090
Yes.

72
00:05:41,174 --> 00:05:42,842
Too bad I wasn't there.

73
00:05:42,925 --> 00:05:45,887
So, when's the wedding?

74
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:48,139
- Actually, I don't know yet.
- But you know,

75
00:05:48,222 --> 00:05:51,559
they say there's a rule.
Once you're engaged,

76
00:05:51,642 --> 00:05:53,770
the wedding should be within a year.

77
00:05:53,853 --> 00:05:56,105
Otherwise, they say it won't happen.

78
00:05:57,940 --> 00:06:02,195
You know, after everything Mikoy
and Chiara have been through, nah,

79
00:06:02,278 --> 00:06:04,614
nothing can stop those two

80
00:06:04,697 --> 00:06:06,365
from getting married whenever they want.

81
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:07,450
Um…

82
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:15,333
Of course! Why wouldn't you be?

83
00:06:15,416 --> 00:06:16,834
Besides,

84
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:19,629
Mom and Dad would be thrilled to see you.

85
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:26,177
You remember that one summer
we spent together?

86
00:06:27,011 --> 00:06:32,183
That whole vacation
we spent together in Tortahan?

87
00:06:32,266 --> 00:06:34,560
That was when

88
00:06:35,561 --> 00:06:37,688
we truly considered you

89
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:42,735
a full-fledged Pinagpala!

90
00:06:42,819 --> 00:06:43,986
High five!

91
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,947
You're officially a Pinagpala!

92
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:49,158
You're truly part of the family!

93
00:06:50,618 --> 00:06:51,494
Right?

94
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:56,582
I'm proud to be a Pinagpala!

95
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:58,543
Well then,

96
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:00,628
I have to head to class.

97
00:07:21,023 --> 00:07:22,358
Chiara, come join us.

98
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:24,485
Last is 1, 2. Just for fun.

99
00:07:27,029 --> 00:07:28,948
This is just minimal.

100
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:29,866
It's fun.

101
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:31,492
Maybe next time.

102
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:37,206
Here, sweetheart.

103
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:39,542
There!

104
00:07:39,625 --> 00:07:40,543
Better?

105
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:43,963
What's wrong?

106
00:07:45,381 --> 00:07:50,136
I'm just making sure your proposal
wasn't just a dream.

107
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:53,514
You know what the most
convincing evidence is?

108
00:07:53,598 --> 00:07:54,599
Your hangover.

109
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:57,393
You had way too much fun.

110
00:07:57,477 --> 00:08:00,146
You partied a little too hard, sweetheart.

111
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:02,815
I deserve to be happy.

112
00:08:03,441 --> 00:08:07,111
It's my first time ever feeling
this normal.

113
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:08,863
It's my first time getting drunk.

114
00:08:10,281 --> 00:08:11,199
That's true.

115
00:08:11,782 --> 00:08:13,576
Good for you, sweetheart.

116
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:15,828
But…

117
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:18,998
Do you remember what you did?

118
00:08:20,541 --> 00:08:24,962
Chiara!

119
00:08:25,046 --> 00:08:28,424
Chiara!

120
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,676
You were amazing last night!

121
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,512
It felt like we were at a club!

122
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:33,471
Awesome!

123
00:08:35,932 --> 00:08:37,058
Did I hurt anyone?

124
00:08:37,141 --> 00:08:38,643
Did I hurt you?

125
00:08:38,726 --> 00:08:40,019
Did I kill anyone?

126
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:41,812
Whoa, straight to killing?

127
00:08:41,896 --> 00:08:44,607
Everything's fine, sweetheart.
Nothing happened, okay?

128
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:46,108
You're something else.

129
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:49,153
Why do I feel like that's not all I did?

130
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:53,449
Not really.

131
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,368
You just made a few impulsive decisions.

132
00:08:57,912 --> 00:08:59,580
You really don't remember?

133
00:09:00,748 --> 00:09:03,125
No! What did I do?

134
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:12,760
What?

135
00:09:30,361 --> 00:09:31,362
You know what he told me?

136
00:09:31,445 --> 00:09:35,324
He said she already considers me
a true Pinagpala.

137
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:37,535
Wow! A sibling.

138
00:09:37,618 --> 00:09:39,704
A family member.

139
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:42,456
What am I, a TV network?

140
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:43,666
Seriously!

141
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,252
I really thought

142
00:09:46,335 --> 00:09:49,672
our relationship had reached
a whole new level.

143
00:09:49,755 --> 00:09:52,174
After what happened.

144
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:03,144
<i>But after summer, when we</i>
<i>came back to school…</i>

145
00:10:03,227 --> 00:10:05,730
<i>Poof! Back to nothing!</i>

146
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:07,189
<i>Like nothing happened.</i>

147
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:09,650
<i>Isn't that so annoying?</i>

148
00:10:11,944 --> 00:10:13,446
Sorry.

149
00:10:13,529 --> 00:10:17,825
For dumping all my frustrations on you.

150
00:10:17,908 --> 00:10:23,497
I obviously can't vent to Angelito
because he's the source of my angst.

151
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:28,502
But you know,
I wish he were more like Bogs.

152
00:10:28,586 --> 00:10:31,297
He ended up dating his best friend.

153
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:33,716
- Something like that. Right?
- Sofie.

154
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:36,969
Who are you talking to now?

155
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:39,347
No one, no one.

156
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:42,016
I was just memorizing something.

157
00:10:42,099 --> 00:10:45,353
See? I'm studying for our lesson.

158
00:10:45,436 --> 00:10:47,188
We have an exam.

159
00:10:56,530 --> 00:10:57,531
Stuff like that.

160
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:59,742
Since when did you take
grade school science?

161
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:03,245
Wait, what are you doing here?

162
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:04,372
Don't you have class?

163
00:11:05,289 --> 00:11:06,290
Nothing.

164
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:09,043
I just wanted to hang out with you.

165
00:11:12,463 --> 00:11:13,839
Wait, wait, hold on.

166
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:16,592
Can I ask you something?

167
00:11:19,845 --> 00:11:21,347
Do you like me?

168
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:31,399
I was trying to stop you.

169
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:34,402
I thought you were making
another impulsive decision.

170
00:11:34,485 --> 00:11:36,654
Then you suddenly snatched my phone.

171
00:11:36,737 --> 00:11:40,408
You were the one who offered
Alex the maid of honor role, sweetheart.

172
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:46,414
Well, Alex did become
a good friend of ours

173
00:11:46,497 --> 00:11:48,958
after everything with La Morte Bianca.

174
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:57,174
What are you saying?

175
00:12:00,344 --> 00:12:02,721
I think she'd make a good maid of honor.

176
00:12:08,894 --> 00:12:11,522
Have you forgotten
what you told me before?

177
00:12:15,359 --> 00:12:17,903
I know how painful it is

178
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:19,905
when the man I love

179
00:12:20,531 --> 00:12:22,867
doesn't feel the same way.

180
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,957
<i>It gets wounded so easily.</i>

181
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:33,335
And can easily be hurt.

182
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:37,214
Well, maybe she was just

183
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:41,135
protective of you before
because you’re an asset.

184
00:12:41,218 --> 00:12:43,304
And most likely,

185
00:12:44,013 --> 00:12:45,097
she already moved on.

186
00:12:46,557 --> 00:12:47,725
I like you.

187
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:50,519
<i>I have feelings for you.</i>

188
00:12:52,062 --> 00:12:53,856
I think I'm in love with you.

189
00:12:55,107 --> 00:12:55,941
Wait a second.

190
00:12:56,025 --> 00:12:57,860
I'm the one with the headache, right?

191
00:12:57,943 --> 00:12:59,028
Oh, right.

192
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,072
Maybe.

193
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:08,078
Also,

194
00:13:09,747 --> 00:13:11,999
I just don't have anyone to invite.

195
00:13:15,294 --> 00:13:19,340
Honestly, I don't even know
who to invite to my wedding.

196
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:23,844
My mom and dad are in prison,

197
00:13:24,762 --> 00:13:27,306
and I don't have any friends here.

198
00:13:30,726 --> 00:13:33,312
What about your friends in Prague?

199
00:13:33,979 --> 00:13:34,813
Right?

200
00:13:36,482 --> 00:13:39,068
I grew up under La Morte Bianca.

201
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:43,489
Do you really think I made
any friends there?

202
00:13:45,241 --> 00:13:48,661
The only one I got close to was Donatello,

203
00:13:48,744 --> 00:13:52,873
and I don't even know what corner
of the world I'd find him in.

204
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:55,125
So,

205
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:59,046
Alex is the only one I can invite.

206
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:01,173
Ironically,

207
00:14:02,299 --> 00:14:05,052
she and Sianong are the only people
I can truly call my friends.

208
00:14:12,726 --> 00:14:14,728
GLOBAL AGENCY FOR GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS

209
00:14:14,812 --> 00:14:16,272
Hello, sir. Good morning.

210
00:14:16,355 --> 00:14:18,357
Are you looking for Sir Norberto?

211
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:19,650
No, no.

212
00:14:19,733 --> 00:14:21,777
- He's not here. He stepped out.
- Oh.

213
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:22,945
Just ask for help.

214
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:24,405
I’ll handle it.

215
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:25,322
Sir?

216
00:14:41,297 --> 00:14:42,715
Have you seen Agent Alex?

217
00:14:42,798 --> 00:14:43,841
Agent Alex?

218
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:45,885
She was just at her desk earlier.

219
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:47,553
She might've stepped out.

220
00:14:47,636 --> 00:14:49,930
No, because when I passed by, I saw…

221
00:15:04,653 --> 00:15:06,322
Okay, okay. I'll be right there.

222
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:20,210
Bok.

223
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:22,546
If I didn't know you,

224
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:26,717
I'd think you were a criminal
running from the law.

225
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:30,512
You know I'm avoiding our beloved senator.

226
00:15:31,096 --> 00:15:31,931
Why?

227
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:33,766
Is he still bothering you?

228
00:15:33,849 --> 00:15:36,101
Is he still pressuring you

229
00:15:36,185 --> 00:15:39,146
to recruit Mikoy and Chiara
to work for us?

230
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:41,148
You can say that again.

231
00:15:42,816 --> 00:15:43,776
Bok.

232
00:15:44,818 --> 00:15:47,112
You know you can always

233
00:15:47,696 --> 00:15:50,240
tell Director Norberto
and report it, right?

234
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:53,077
You know our director
gets pressured easily.

235
00:16:05,714 --> 00:16:07,257
And if they end up

236
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:10,719
turning it down because they really
don't want to work with us,

237
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:11,637
then you're good.

238
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:13,389
Senator Quintin can't do anything.

239
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:16,350
He can't force people
to do what they don't want.

240
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:24,858
But now isn't the right time
to tell Mikoy and Chiara.

241
00:16:26,777 --> 00:16:27,611
Why?

242
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:40,374
What?

243
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:42,167
Chiara?

244
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:50,843
Mikoy and Chiara are getting married.

245
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:54,471
What will happen in the next chapter?

246
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:58,267
It's finally happening. How exciting!

247
00:16:58,350 --> 00:17:00,227
Uh… Oh, someone's jealous.

248
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:02,563
You're in trouble now.

249
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:04,481
She's getting married.

250
00:17:04,565 --> 00:17:06,108
- She's getting married.
- Sit down already.

251
00:17:13,907 --> 00:17:15,367
- Mikoy, Chiara, come here!
- Tess!

252
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:16,827
- Mom!
- It's Tess.

253
00:17:16,910 --> 00:17:18,120
She wants you to meet someone.

254
00:17:18,203 --> 00:17:19,288
- Come here.
- Mom.

255
00:17:29,506 --> 00:17:31,133
- Hello.
- Hello, Chiara.

256
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:33,302
I'm your mother's friend.

257
00:17:33,385 --> 00:17:36,221
So when I heard
you two were getting married,

258
00:17:36,305 --> 00:17:39,308
well, I offered my services.

259
00:17:39,391 --> 00:17:41,602
Services for what?

260
00:17:41,685 --> 00:17:44,063
Well, in case you didn't know,
I'm a wedding planner,

261
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:48,150
and I'm sure you're going to need
my expertise

262
00:17:48,233 --> 00:17:50,444
to make your dream wedding come true.

263
00:17:50,527 --> 00:17:51,820
That's right! That's right!

264
00:17:51,904 --> 00:17:52,780
So that's it.

265
00:17:52,863 --> 00:17:56,116
I've planned every politician's wedding
here in our town.

266
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:59,078
From the lowliest councilor

267
00:17:59,161 --> 00:18:00,913
all the way up to the governor.

268
00:18:00,996 --> 00:18:02,706
I handled every single one of them!

269
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:05,250
Mass weddings?

270
00:18:06,502 --> 00:18:07,878
Mock weddings?

271
00:18:08,962 --> 00:18:10,506
Dog and cat weddings?

272
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:11,632
Double check!

273
00:18:11,715 --> 00:18:13,801
I've handled every kind
of wedding there is.

274
00:18:14,384 --> 00:18:15,469
She's done them all.

275
00:18:17,387 --> 00:18:20,057
Hold on. Tell them
about that one wedding you planned.

276
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:21,433
Well, here goes.

277
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:24,478
I once helped a couple get married.

278
00:18:24,561 --> 00:18:27,022
Nothing special. It was a simple wedding.

279
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:28,690
They were just an ordinary couple.

280
00:18:28,774 --> 00:18:31,235
But on their wedding day, a storm hit.

281
00:18:31,318 --> 00:18:32,361
Oh, no!

282
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:33,445
It was a total disaster.

283
00:18:33,529 --> 00:18:34,780
Goodness!

284
00:18:34,863 --> 00:18:38,450
Any other wedding planner
would've canceled,

285
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:40,077
postponed, and packed everything up.

286
00:18:41,745 --> 00:18:44,331
But me? Well, no!

287
00:18:44,414 --> 00:18:45,833
No way.

288
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:47,459
The wedding went on.

289
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:49,169
So there they were,

290
00:18:49,753 --> 00:18:53,048
getting married while
the church was completely flooded.

291
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:55,008
Then, for the wedding march…

292
00:18:56,635 --> 00:18:58,971
they walked through the floodwaters.

293
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:02,599
Floodwaters, okay?
Real floodwaters, not AI.

294
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:05,811
But after that,

295
00:19:05,894 --> 00:19:08,105
they posted it on social media.

296
00:19:08,188 --> 00:19:10,649
Boom! It went super viral!

297
00:19:10,732 --> 00:19:12,025
From that alone,

298
00:19:12,109 --> 00:19:15,612
they earned enough to cover
all their wedding expenses.

299
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:16,905
And mind you,

300
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:19,408
they even became endorsers for rain boots

301
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:21,952
and multivitamins against leptospirosis.

302
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:23,787
- How amazing is that?
- Isn't that fabulous?

303
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,247
Absolutely, ma'am!

304
00:19:27,332 --> 00:19:30,544
By the way,
leptospirosis is life-threatening,

305
00:19:30,627 --> 00:19:34,548
so if you experience symptoms
such as fever,

306
00:19:34,631 --> 00:19:37,926
vomiting, chills,

307
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,845
muscle pain, and redness,

308
00:19:39,928 --> 00:19:41,889
especially in your legs and calves,

309
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:44,224
and loss of appetite,

310
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:48,896
go to the nearest hospital immediately.

311
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:50,647
Just remember,

312
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:52,441
don't wade through floodwaters,

313
00:19:53,025 --> 00:19:54,818
and keep your wounds covered.

314
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:57,070
- That's right.
- Exactly.

315
00:19:57,154 --> 00:19:58,947
- Don't let them get wet.
- Right.

316
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:10,667
That's right!

317
00:20:12,127 --> 00:20:13,378
Well said!

318
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:15,047
What do you think, kids?

319
00:20:15,130 --> 00:20:16,924
Mikoy? Chiara?

320
00:20:20,719 --> 00:20:21,845
That's right!

321
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:24,514
We need all the help we can get,

322
00:20:24,598 --> 00:20:28,143
especially since we don't know
where or how to begin.

323
00:20:32,522 --> 00:20:33,607
Let's plan a wedding!

324
00:20:41,949 --> 00:20:43,075
Well…

325
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:47,120
This is the latest trend.

326
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:51,166
Cheapness?

327
00:20:52,584 --> 00:20:53,835
Look at this guy.

328
00:20:56,797 --> 00:21:00,133
Because all of us
return to where we began.

329
00:21:00,217 --> 00:21:05,180
Our ancestors
lived and made their homes in caves.

330
00:21:05,764 --> 00:21:09,518
And that's where the cradle
of civilization began.

331
00:21:09,601 --> 00:21:10,644
Simple!

332
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:18,068
Two souls always drawn

333
00:21:19,152 --> 00:21:20,153
to each other.

334
00:21:20,237 --> 00:21:22,614
As if they're a perfect match!

335
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:24,825
Like a stalagmite and a stalactite!

336
00:21:26,743 --> 00:21:27,953
So, guys?

337
00:21:30,914 --> 00:21:31,957
Um…

338
00:21:33,625 --> 00:21:36,169
It's okay. It's just…

339
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:39,881
I can't picture it.

340
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:51,351
Instead of wearing a gown,
you'll be dressed as Batgirl.

341
00:21:53,186 --> 00:21:56,690
And you, Mikoy,
you won't be wearing a barong.

342
00:21:57,274 --> 00:22:00,068
You'll be dressed as Batman!

343
00:22:00,944 --> 00:22:02,154
Right?

344
00:22:02,237 --> 00:22:05,115
Now that's what you call forever!

345
00:22:06,616 --> 00:22:10,287
Because Batgirl and Batman
will get married in the…

346
00:22:14,958 --> 00:22:16,251
That actually sounds nice.

347
00:22:17,419 --> 00:22:19,004
Then Robin can be my best man!

348
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:21,840
That would be amazing, sweetheart!

349
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:26,970
It's just…

350
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:28,472
It doesn't really suit us.

351
00:22:29,973 --> 00:22:32,768
Do you have any other options?

352
00:22:42,903 --> 00:22:45,489
I gave you all those ideas,
and you didn't like a single one.

353
00:22:46,531 --> 00:22:47,741
Fine.

354
00:22:47,824 --> 00:22:48,950
Let's think of something else.

355
00:22:49,993 --> 00:22:51,495
Where are the bats around here?

356
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:53,121
Maybe they're the ones
who want to get married.

357
00:23:08,011 --> 00:23:10,472
Sir. You wanted to see me?

358
00:23:23,902 --> 00:23:26,071
Do you know what that means?

359
00:23:28,365 --> 00:23:33,370
It means I'll have to let go
half of our personnel,

360
00:23:33,453 --> 00:23:35,330
starting today!

361
00:23:51,054 --> 00:23:54,182
Did Senator Quintin tell you anything?

362
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:57,519
I saw the two of you talking
several days ago.

363
00:23:59,729 --> 00:24:01,022
No, sir.

364
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:08,864
You know I can always tell
when you're lying.

365
00:24:08,947 --> 00:24:11,324
What's going on, Alex?

366
00:24:13,451 --> 00:24:14,494
Um…

367
00:24:15,245 --> 00:24:19,583
Sir, maybe it's related to the fact
that Senator Quintin wants

368
00:24:20,208 --> 00:24:22,878
Mikoy and Chiara to rejoin our agency.

369
00:24:25,714 --> 00:24:28,341
Why? Haven't they done enough already?

370
00:24:29,301 --> 00:24:31,344
That's exactly what I told him,

371
00:24:31,428 --> 00:24:33,763
but he insisted that we convince

372
00:24:33,847 --> 00:24:35,891
the two of them to return
to law enforcement.

373
00:24:35,974 --> 00:24:37,058
And what did you say?

374
00:24:45,066 --> 00:24:46,568
Is there a problem, sir?

375
00:24:48,069 --> 00:24:49,529
It just got me thinking…

376
00:24:51,573 --> 00:24:54,492
Why would Senator Quintin want to do that?

377
00:24:55,368 --> 00:24:58,705
I mean, there's no reason
to recruit Mikoy and Chiara.

378
00:25:04,127 --> 00:25:08,298
Unless they're trying
to form a kill squad.

379
00:25:14,721 --> 00:25:17,807
Who do they want to eliminate?

380
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:33,156
We all gather here today
to solve a very pressing issue.

381
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:37,202
Whether Agent alex will agree
to become the maid of honor

382
00:25:37,285 --> 00:25:39,204
in Mikoy and Chiara’s wedding.

383
00:25:39,287 --> 00:25:40,830
But you know--

384
00:25:41,581 --> 00:25:42,666
Don’t say anything.

385
00:25:45,335 --> 00:25:47,879
Actually, I talked to Mikoy earlier.

386
00:25:50,465 --> 00:25:51,299
<i>What’s wrong?</i>

387
00:25:51,383 --> 00:25:53,969
<i>I just remember my Dad and Mom.</i>

388
00:25:54,052 --> 00:25:55,512
And to be honest,

389
00:25:55,595 --> 00:25:58,765
they’re responsible for all the bad things
that have happened in my life.

390
00:25:58,848 --> 00:26:01,101
But everytime I see myself

391
00:26:01,184 --> 00:26:02,686
saying my vows

392
00:26:02,769 --> 00:26:04,229
infront of the altar,

393
00:26:04,312 --> 00:26:06,606
they should be there, right?

394
00:26:10,402 --> 00:26:12,070
- Alex?
- Why?

395
00:26:12,153 --> 00:26:13,238
Are we okay?

396
00:26:13,321 --> 00:26:16,032
Is this about what I told you, Mikoy?

397
00:26:16,116 --> 00:26:17,325
Yes.

398
00:26:17,409 --> 00:26:18,660
You know what, Mikoy?

399
00:26:18,743 --> 00:26:20,704
<i>I just wanted to tell you the truth.</i>

400
00:26:20,787 --> 00:26:22,914
But I’m not expecting anything from you.
